    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPrice : Rs. 25.00Postage : Rs. 150.00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n[Bill No. 171]\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nBETTING AND GAMING LEVY (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Betting and Gaming Levy Act, No. 40 of 1988\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPresented by the Minister of Finance, Economic Stabilization& National Policies on 04th of April, 2023\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n(Published in the Gazette on March 24, 2023)\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 2 of the Betting and Gaming Levy Act, No. 40of 1988 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) and the legal effect of thesection as amended is to\u2013\n\n(a)increase the levy on the gross collection from persons carrying on the businessof bookmaker or the business of gaming;\n\n(b)dissuade a citizen of Sri Lanka from entering a place of business of gaming bycharging a casino entrance levy of United States dollars fifty; and\n\n(c)provide for the liability of a person who fails to collect and pay the levies underthis Act.\n\nClause 3 : This clause amends section 2A of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section as amended is to provide for the requirement to obtain a license and for theregistration with the Department of Inland Revenue in respect of a person who carries onthe business of gaming and business of a bookmaker.\n\nClause 4 : This clause amends section 4 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof the section as amended is to\u2013\n\n(a)provide for the payments of the levy on the gross collection and for the casinoentrance levy on instalments as provided for other levies; and\n\n(b)extend the application of certain provisions of the Inland Revenue Act, No. 24of 2017 being consequential to the application of clause 3."
