    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Prime Minister and Minister of Public Administration,Home Affairs, Provincial Councils and Local Government on 18th of October, 2022\n\n(Published in the Gazette on September 27, 2022)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPrice : Rs. 12.00Postage : Rs. 15.00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n[Bill No. 155]\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nBILL\n\nA\n\nVALUE ADDED TAX (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Value Added Tax Act, No. 14 of 2002\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 2 of the Value Added Tax Act, No. 14 of 2002(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d), and the legal effect of that section asamended is to increase the VAT rate\u2013\n\n(i) from 8% to 12% with effect from June 1, 2022 to August 31, 2022; and\n\n(ii) from 12% to 15% with effect from September 1, 2022,\n\non the value of goods or services supplied, or goods imported.\n\nClause 3 : This clause amends section 10 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof that section as amended is to decrease the threshold of registration for VAT fromRs. 300 million to Rs. 80 million per annum with effect from October 1, 2022.\n\nClause 4 : This clause amends Part II of the First Schedule to the principal enactment inorder to remove the VAT exemption on condominium residential apartments with effectfrom October 1, 2022.\n\nValue Added Tax (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\nL. D.\u2014 O. 16/2022\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE VALUE ADDED TAX ACT, NO. 14 OF 2002\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Value Added Tax(Amendment) Act, No. of 2022.\n\n2.Section 2 of the Value Added Tax Act, No.14 of 2002(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is herebyamended as follows:-"
